schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W-ASSERTION-ACK-SLAVEADDR-VACUOUS
  failure_class: assertion_checker
  failure_mechanism: 'incorrect_sampling_phase: the error-severity checker ack_error_implies_unsupported_address
    samples the released slave_addr stimulus pin at the done edge; the driver restores
    slave_addr to 0x00 immediately after the request-latch edge and the done pulse
    fires ~4 edges later (CONTRACT.md section 6), so the pin always reads 0x00 and
    the check can never fire on DUT NACK behavior - a structural no-op still counted
    as an active error checker'
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: tb/assertions.py lines 292-314 fail only when pins.slave_addr
    equals 0x50 at a done+ack_error edge; because I2CDriver._offer -> release_inputs
    (driver.py lines 88-92) drives slave_addr to 0x00 right after the request-latch
    edge, every sampled value at completion is 0x00, so the assertion is vacuous for
    DUT ack-error correlation and only an (undesirable) stimulus mis-drive could ever
    trip it. The weakness report's code evidence, the checker docstring's own admission,
    and the '6 active checkers, violations -> none' logs all agree.
  consequence: 'A DUT that NACKs the supported slave 0x50 (or mis-correlates ack_error
    with the latched address) would pass all 16 tests while the report claims the
    plan-mandated error-severity guard ''On done with ack_error == 1: slave_addr !=
    0x50'' is active; the reported assertion strength is overstated and the property
    is left to the scoreboard alone.'
candidate_interventions:
- Reimplement _check_ack_error_implies_unsupported_address to capture slave_addr at
  the request-latch point (start==1 while busy==0 on a rising edge, i.e. where the
  DUT FSM latches the stimulus, mirroring I2CMonitor's sampling discipline) and evaluate
  done+ack_error against that latched address (selected).
- Subscribe the assertion to the monitor's I2CTransaction analysis stream so the done
  pulse is paired with the monitor-reconstructed latched address; more coupling and
  requires rewiring env.py connect_phase.
- Demote the vacuous checker to a documented no-op / remove it so the end-of-test
  report stops counting it as an active DUT check (acceptable fallback, reduces reported
  checker strength).
- 'Defer W-ORACLE-UNSUPPORTED-READDATA: restoring the read_data==0x00 oracle in both
  scoring paths was already attempted in iteration 1 and rejected (1 test failed because
  the current RTL genuinely retains stale read_data per documented I2C_DISC_001);
  no RTL repair or owner re-scope has occurred, so re-attempting is not justified.'
- 'Defer W-SCENARIO-OPENDRAIN-CHECKS-DROPPED: re-adding START-like/access-phase bus
  checks needs a mid-transaction bus trace and reworking the tb_top continuous pull-up
  drive; cannot be validated RTL-blind and risks breaking the existing bus-idle release
  checks.'
selected_intervention:
  type: reimplement_vacuous_assertion_to_correlate_done_with_request_latch_address
  expected_effect:
  - 'The assertion becomes a genuine error-severity DUT check: done+ack_error==1 is
    compared against the slave address actually latched at request time, so a supported-address
    (0x50) NACK is detected.'
  - Remains silent on the current RTL - the plan's I2C_DISC notes document ack_error
    only for unsupported addresses - so all 16 regression tests stay green (no acceptance-criteria
    violation).
  - The end-of-test report's 'violations -> none' becomes a true statement about an
    implemented property rather than a vacuous no-op, restoring consistency between
    CONTRACT.md's useful_assertions claim and the code.
  - Done-edge evaluation takes precedence over offer latching, so a done-pulse coinciding
    with the next back-to-back offer is checked against the prior latched address,
    and reset injection clears the latched state.
regression_risks:
- Latched-address capture could in principle mis-pair done+ack_error with a stale
  offer and raise spuriously; mitigated by using the monitor's proven edge discipline
  and clearing the latch on reset - the current RTL cannot trip it because supported
  0x50 never produces ack_error.
- 'If a runtime sampling race were ever observed (e.g. a spurious failure in the randomized
  test), fall back to the documented alternative: demote the checker to warning severity
  or remove it so the report stops overstating assertion strength.'
validation:
- Run the full 16-test regression (make regression); all tests must pass with zero
  scoreboard mismatches and zero assertion failures.
- Confirm I2C_07/I2C_08/I2C_09 and the corner unsupported scenarios now traverse the
  real check path (done+ack_error sampled against latched unsupported addresses),
  so the pass is achieved through genuine evaluation, not pin vacuity.
- Inspect logs/checker counters on I2CRandomizedTest to verify no assertion failure
  across reset-injection and back-to-back offers; confirm no other component depends
  on the old pin-sampling behavior.

