schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W_04
  failure_class: coverage_accuracy
  failure_mechanism: 'misleading_bins: tb/coverage.py sample_transaction() samples
    write_data_cp and read_data_cp from every monitor item without gating by transaction
    semantics, so driver don''t-care defaults are binned as if exercised - read transactions''
    default write_data=0 fills data_0x00 with no write of 0x00 ever occurring (I2C02
    log shows write_data_cp=2/4 after exactly one 0xAA write plus one read), and supported-address
    writes contribute stale/unspecified read_data bytes to read_data_cp; this reports
    coverage for stimulus that was never driven, masking real holes'
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: 'write_data_cp/read_data_cp coverpoints are contaminated by don''t-care
    defaults: rw==1 items sample write_data=0 into data_0x00, and rw==0 supported
    writes sample stale/unspecified read_data into read-pattern bins, so the 100%
    coverage number includes bins that were never genuinely exercised (verified in
    tb/coverage.py:234-264 and simulation log cited in weakness report)'
  consequence: Coverage metrics misstate what stimulus actually occurred; the data_0x00
    write bin can appear covered without a single write of 0x00, and read-pattern
    bins can be filled by stale don't-care bytes, so functional coverage cannot expose
    real stimulus holes and the plan's coverage intent (cover exercised write/read
    patterns) is not honored
candidate_interventions:
- Restore the spec-mandated read_data==0x00 oracle for unsupported-address transactions
  in I2CScoreboard and I2CRandomizedSequence plus a non-vacuous directed case (W_01)
  - rejected in iteration 1 (1 test failed) because it surfaces the genuine documented
  RTL defect I2C_DISC_001; as a TB-only change it cannot keep the regression green,
  so repeating it is not justified
- Re-instrument I2C_12 to assert START-like/access-phase low drives with corrected
  pull-up modeling (W_02) - observability of DUT-driven lows is not available under
  the constant scl/sda=1 pull-up drive and pure-Python/Verilator resolution; high
  risk of turning I2C_12 red, deferred
- Add a read-after-reset detection scenario for I2C_DISC_002 (W_03) - a hard-failing
  check would redden the regression against the documented RTL memory-retention divergence;
  a report-only variant is defensible but a larger, judgment-heavy change, deferred
- Gate write_data_cp/read_data_cp coverage sampling by transaction semantics so only
  fields with defined meaning are binned (W_04, selected)
selected_intervention:
  type: coverage_sampling_gated_by_transaction_semantics
  expected_effect:
  - write_data_cp is sampled only for rw==0 transactions, so bins reflect actual write-data
    stimulus and data_0x00 can no longer be filled by a read's default write_data=0
  - read_data_cp is sampled only where read_data has defined semantics (supported-address
    reads and unsupported-address transaction results, mirroring CONTRACT.md section
    12.6 comparison scope), eliminating stale/don't-care byte contamination from supported
    writes
  - All four bins of both coverpoints remain hit across the existing 16-test regression
    (writes 0x00/0xFF/0x55/0xAA and matching read-back/unsupported 0x00 results are
    all exercised in directed and corner tests), so functional coverage stays at 100%
    and the three crosses are unaffected
  - 'Pass/fail behavior is unchanged: I2CCoverage is observation-only and never raises
    on the DUT''s behalf; the change is confined to tb/coverage.py sampling gating'
regression_risks:
- 'No test-failure risk: the fix only changes which monitor items feed two coverpoints;
  no checker, scoreboard, or driver path is touched and coverage components never
  affect pass/fail'
